          "optimizationTarget": null,
          "locked": false,
          "description": "Two-beam Fizeau approximation. Monochromatic 632.8 nm, collimated Gaussian beam diameter 4 mm. A 50:50 pickup cube sends light along +Z and sends both returns to the same Camera. Reference flat: ideal AR entrance Z=75 mm, 5 mm N-BK7, 4% reflecting rear reference face Z=80 mm. Test face nominal Z=100 mm, reflectance 4%, tilt X=0.02 deg. Both beams traverse the reference substrate twice; physical cavity OPD is 40 mm on axis when parallel. The flat BeamSplitter uses a local 45-degree coating normal: rotation Y=-135 deg makes the physical reference face normal to global Z, not oblique. Fixed R/T and scalar phase; first reflected pair only, no higher cavity orders, polarization or coating-stack model. Treat the source as a coherent monochromatic laser with coherence length greater than 40 mm. Run Coherent Signal after each change. No surface-height inversion or grating calibration is claimed."
        },
